{
  "title": "Grilled Asparagus",
  "description": "Grilled asparagus with olive oil, lemon, and a hint of spice.",
  "servings": "4 serving(s)",
  "instructions": "Wash the asparagus and pat dry thoroughly. Using a sharp knife, cut about 1-inch from the base of the asparagus stalks and discard.\n\nCombine the trimmed asparagus, olive oil, salt, and pepper in a large bowl or on a rimmed sheet pan. Toss until the asparagus is well coated.\n\nPreheat the grill to medium high heat (400 to 450°). Add the asparagus to the grill, placing them crosswise on the grill grates so that they don't fall through. Grill, turning as needed, until grill marks form, 3 to 4 minutes per side.\n\nTransfer the asparagus to a serving platter; squeeze one lemon half over the asparagus. Sprinkle with red pepper flakes and more salt and pepper, if you like.",
